# BRAN Org - Dual Open Science & Open Data License

This organization and its repositories are licensed under a dual-licensing structure to guarantee software freedom (Open Source Copyleft) and open scientific data interoperability (Open Access / Open Data).

---

## 1. Software & Codebase License: GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)

All source code, engine scripts, web interfaces, backend servers, components, and automated workflows developed by BRAN Org are licensed under the **GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)** or any later version.

### Summary of Rights:
- **Freedom to run**: You may run the software for any purpose (academic, scientific, personal, commercial).
- **Freedom to study and modify**: You can inspect and alter the code to suit your needs.
- **Copyleft / Open Science Guarantee**: Any derivative work or modified version of this software engine MUST also be distributed under the GPL-3.0 license and remain 100% open source.

For full license terms, see: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html

---

## 2. Scientific Dataset & Metadata License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

All scientific datasets, article metadata, JSON databases, CSV exports, and scientometric schemas provided by BRAN Org (under `data/` directories or served via REST API endpoints) are licensed under the **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)** license.

### Summary of Rights:
- **Share**: Copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format.
- **Adapt**: Remix, transform, and build upon the material for any purpose, including academic research, AI model training, scientometric analyses, and commercial indexing.
- **Attribution**: You must give appropriate credit to BRAN Org and the original source (e.g., ABEC Brasil / EBBC), provide a link to the license, and indicate if changes were made.

For full license terms, see: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode

